A||||5||kslish||Indy 500 -  Who's your favorite?||||1||
Z||000000||kslish||05-26-2001||11:19 PM||||Okay, so it's about 13 hours till they announce "Gentlemen and lady, please start your engines" (remember, there is a female in the field this year) at the Indy 500.  Anybody have a favorite to win?  I've got it narrowed down to a few I'd like to see win.:<P>1.) Gil deFerran - current CART world champion, drives for "the Captain" himself (Roger Penske) who has won 10 Indy 500's as a car owner....Penske knows the strategy needed to win like no other.<P>2.) Arie Luyendyk - sentimetal favorite since he came out of retirement just for this race (not to mention he's still pretty fast). <P>3.) Tony Stewart - just because he can drive the heck out of anything with a motor and four wheels.  It would be also quite interesting to see him leave victory lane and fly to Charlotte for the NASCAR race he's also planning on running tomorrow (he insists that he will drink milk and run if needed to).  <P>After that, probably any CART driver....just because I'm not a fan of Tony George and his attitude towards CART and their drivers.<P>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
