Z||000002||Tweek||05-27-2001||11:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B> <A HREF="http://www.teamcheever.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.teamcheever.com/</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya know...  Some how I figured that||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||05-27-2001||04:30 PM||||Okay, so I picked the wrong Penske driver.  I never expected a rookie to win two years in a row, reguardless of the series he came from.<P>I wonder what Tony George is going to do now (i.e. rule changes) now that Roger Penske was so dominant finishing 1-2 with his cars and Michael Andretti and Chip Ganassi's drivers filling up the 3rd through 6th positions.  After this performance, I wouldn't be surprised to see the entire CART series showing up at Indianapolis next year with cars....which is what it should be, the best open wheel drivers in the world (save maybe for F1, but they don't do ovals) converging every year at Indianapolis.  The whole CART vs. IRL thing can make the Indy 500 the superbowl of open wheel racing which will only make the race more exciting like it was this year....just as long as the IRL plays nice and welcomes the extra competition in the future.<P>Well gotta tune in and see if Tony Stewart is going to make it to Charlotte in time for the 600.....<P>P.S. - When is Cheever going to quit using Infinity engines so he can last all 500 miles?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 05-27-2001).]||||reg||1
