Z||000005||Eric||05-27-2001||11:11 PM||||Isn't it obvious the best open wheel racers in the country haven't been at the Brickyard for the second half of the last decade.  Tony George shouldn't try to run a second rate organization like this.  The teams in the IRL are going to lose sponsorships like crazy, and there's nothing he can do about it.  The Indy 500 is officially a joke.  Did anyone see Stephen Tyler sing the national anthum?  What a clown..  CART (and Roger Penske) can justifiably make the statement they have the best open wheel racers in the country, and second only to F1 in the world.  We'll see the IRL fold within the next three years.  Guys like Arie, who couldn't drive a road circuit to save his life, and girls like Sarah, who is propped up by the people around her only to make stupid mistakes time after time (She is the perpetual rookie) will be household names no longer.  Long live racing.||||reg||1
